Subject: [#94-8-165] CPSR Annual Meeting - Oct. 8-9, San Diego

My fellow 'tropes --

The Computer Professionals for Social Responsibility (CPSR) is gaining
significant prominence; they have been instrumental in a lot of the
anti-Clipper mobilization, for example, and the opposition to the various
Digital Telephony initiatives.

There is a major bug in CPSR, however -- "social responsibility" is defined
as "socialist responsibility".  The organization leans (one might say
"lists") leftward.  This is largely because the libertarian members all
have real jobs in industry, while the lefties are all tenured faculty with
lots of spare time on their hands.

I'd like to get together a road-trip for Bay Area Extropians who are also
CPSR members to attend, and try to influence, the annual meeting described
below.  As you can see, the agenda is markedly left-liberal, and the agenda
for many of the sessions is "How can we get Silicon Valley programmers to
pay for net access for the homeless of Los Angeles?"

Please read the conference program below and consider the idea of attending
the conference.  If you like the idea of exposing these (for lack of a
better word) pinkos to an alternative viewpoint, please reply to me and
let's get a road-trip organized.
                                        dV/dt
P.S. I am cc'ing this to the main list so extropians in other areas can
consider attending, as well.

